Documented cache contract
- `litellm/proxy/proxy_server.py` defines `UserAPIKeyCacheTTLEnum.in_memory_cache_ttl = 60`
- `user_api_key_cache` initializes with that 60-second default
- `general_settings.user_api_key_cache_ttl` overrides both in-memory and Redis TTLs when configured
- `IdentityStore` reads the hashed bearer from `user_api_key_cache` before the database
- `_cache_key_object` writes through `_cache_management_object`, which uses `get_management_object_ttl`
- The disposable config sets no `user_api_key_cache_ttl` and no Redis auth cache, so effective authorization-cache TTL is 60 seconds

